# Runtime artifacts created by bootstrap.sh on a real server.
#
# They only appear here if someone installs from a source checkout rather than
# the release tarball — but this whole folder is mirrored to a PUBLIC repository,
# so the cost of forgetting is permanent and the cost of this file is nothing.

# Encrypted secrets bundle. Encrypted, but an attacker who has it only needs the
# passphrase, and it should live in a password manager rather than a git tree.
tms-secrets-escrow.enc

# Diagnostics archive. Redacted, but generated from live logs.
tms-support-*.tar.gz

# The realm definition is copied in by the release packaging, not committed.
# It already exists in two places that must be kept in step; a third copy in git
# would be a third place to forget.
k3s/tms-realm.json

# Rendered manifests, for inspection before applying.
*.rendered.yaml
